      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5dc5b9b25689666d718db510|full_name}: The Quest version of the game runs on a Snapdragon 835. There are lots of phones with better specs.The Pixel 4 uses a 855 for example. Input can be realized by onscreen buttons and be similar to pc input. And if it only runs in 2D it take even less oomph to run the game. I don't see your problem. All they have to do is modify the input to work on a normal phone and compile it for android. It would be like PC desktop VRChat but on a phone and with all the limitations of the Quest version.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
