      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6b3cc227a56787575ebb4|full_name}: I can see your point, but VRChat is a platform devised towards PC (and VR) users, as they are the most likely to buy a VR headset, which is what VRChat was funded by Steam for. I can see most elements of what you are describing to be playable, however, the controls may perhaps be the most absurd part to implement, because you need to see your screen while you are moving, and complex interactions such as emotes (toggle-able or via menu) and picking up objects would be the hardest to add. \nDon't forget that certain games such as (reference) Minecraft have so much cross-compatibility that it takes wayyy longer to update than if it were a one-two platform game.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
